<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg k_sigma at 1.12 µm in the E. rowelli ocellus (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Euperipatoides rowelli)",
        "Schnakenberg k_sigma at 1.12 µm in the E. rowelli ocellus (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Euperipatoides rowelli morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Euperipatoides rowelli specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Euperipatoides rowelli" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A second independent assessor.",
        "does_not_claim: That 1.12 µm was fitted to a published Turing model of E. rowelli.",
        "does_not_claim: That a successor chronospecies exists (the series is 1/1 and extant).",
        "does_not_claim: That the Couch photograph is an electron micrograph.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Holocene mode count N = floor(100 µm / 1.12 µm) = 89, against N = 0 for a Cambrian predecessor below a 10 µm preservation floor.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pearson r = 0.9915 between continuum σ(k) and an eigenvector-seeded explicit linear PDE on modes 3..31.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: γ = 34122.25342711872 is solved so argmax σ(k) = 2π × 14 on the unit domain, i.e. physical wavelength 1.12 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: E. rowelli ocelli are about 100 µm across, with a lens, a rhabdomeric layer, and screening pigment (Mayer 2006; Kirwan 2018; Ljungholm & Nilsson 2021).",
        "reported_in_source: Photoreceptor centres are about 2–3 µm apart; the 2021 optical mesh uses about 2.5 µm. Kirwan 2018 figures microvilli with a 1 µm scale bar.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics du/dt = a − u + u²v, dv/dt = b − u²v.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system.",
        "transfer_boundary: No source measures a Turing wavelength of 1.12 µm in this species. The length is the slot's detail scale, placed in the microvillus/pigment regime those papers describe.",
        "transfer_boundary: The whole-animal photograph is the CV target. Magnifying the 15.68 µm patch onto the body mask is a visualization, not a claim that skin annuli have period 1.12 µm." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Euperipatoides rowelli (Holocene (Extant))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Euperipatoides" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/euperipatoides_rowelli_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Euperipatoides rowelli; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics du/dt = a − u + u²v, dv/dt = b − u²v. | E. rowelli ocelli are about 100 µm across, with a lens, a rhabdomeric layer, and screening pigment (Mayer 2006; Kirwan 2018; Ljungholm & Nilsson 2021). | Photoreceptor centres are about 2–3 µm apart; the 2021 optical mesh uses about 2.5 µm. Kirwan 2018 figures microvilli with a 1 µm scale bar.; reconstructed_in_script: γ = 34122.25342711872 is solved so argmax σ(k) = 2π × 14 on the unit domain, i.e. physical wavelength 1.12 µm. | Holocene mode count N = floor(100 µm / 1.12 µm) = 89, against N = 0 for a Cambrian predecessor below a 10 µm preservation floor. | Pearson r = 0.9915 between continuum σ(k) and an eigenvector-seeded explicit linear PDE on modes 3..31.; transfer_boundary: No source measures a Turing wavelength of 1.12 µm in this species. The length is the slot's detail scale, placed in the microvillus/pigment regime those papers describe. | The whole-animal photograph is the CV target. Magnifying the 15.68 µm patch onto the body mask is a visualization, not a claim that skin annuli have period 1.12 µm.; does_not_claim: That 1.12 µm was fitted to a published Turing model of E. rowelli. | That the Couch photograph is an electron micrograph. | That a successor chronospecies exists (the series is 1/1 and extant). | A second independent assessor.]; phenomenon_size: 1.1 µm (1.131e-06 m, log10=-5.947 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.1 µm to 2.5 mm): 1.1 µm:euperipatoides-rowelli-bioelectric-polarity, 3.5 µm:euperipatoides-rowelli-vertex-packing, 57 µm:euperipatoides-rowelli-turing-wavelength, 113 µm:euperipatoides-rowelli-clock-wavefront, 254 µm:euperipatoides-rowelli-morphogen-condensation, 311 µm:euperipatoides-rowelli-elastic-buckling, 354 µm:euperipatoides-rowelli-flux-canalization, 495 µm:euperipatoides-rowelli-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.asd.2006.06.003>,
